<task id="062" project="spaarkeai-compose-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-33 compaction over ledger + cross-version persistence (DocumentId+MatterId)</title>
    <phase>6 Memory</phase>
    <gate>startable-now</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W4</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <dependencies>061</dependencies>
    <tags>bff-api, testing</tags>
    <fr>FR-33</fr>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Ensure long Compose sessions use the compacted digest over ledger outputs, and that session state binds to
    `DocumentId + MatterId` (NOT to a specific DOCX version) so it survives Word handoffs. Reopening a document
    after a Word round-trip restores prior decisions + annotations. This rides the redesign-r1 compacted-digest
    mechanism (task 002 — digest compaction generalized to cover outputs, keys verbatim) — Compose consumes it,
    it does not invent a new compaction path.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer familiar with the ADR-040 ledger, the redesign-r1 compacted-digest mechanism, and the
    ChatSession DocumentId binding in Sprk.Bff.Api.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Compose session state is keyed by `DocumentId + MatterId` and survives a DOCX version change; long sessions
    render from the compacted digest over ledger outputs; workspace-scope memory items are excluded from the
    conversation-window compaction by design. Tests prove a version change does not reset session state and the
    digest keys survive verbatim.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      design.md §8: "Compaction — the compacted digest over ledger outputs handles long sessions. Cross-version
      persistence — bound to DocumentId + MatterId, NOT to a specific DOCX version. Survives Word handoffs."
      This task wires Compose sessions to that binding + digest so return-from-Word (Phase 5) restores context.
      Depends on task 061's ledger-query surface for reading prior action history into the restored view.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatHistoryManager.cs" role="reference">Compacted digest over ledger outputs (redesign-r1 task 002) — the compaction mechanism Compose consumes.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs" role="edit">Session rebind + DocumentId binding; ensure keying by DocumentId+MatterId, version-independent.</file>
      <file path="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs" role="reference">Session payload persistence; confirm cross-version key stability.</file>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md" role="spec">§8 Compaction + Cross-version persistence paragraphs.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="061" status="pending">Action-history ledger query — the restored view reads prior actions from it.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Compaction operates over ledger outputs (the compacted digest); no parallel session cache; keys survive verbatim in the digest.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Memory-tier retention: workspace-scope memory items live outside the conversation window and are unaffected by compaction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">`Services/Compose/` reaches the ledger/digest via allowed seams only (Tier-1 NetArchTest).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">Session state binds to `DocumentId + MatterId`, NOT to a DOCX version; reopening after a Word round-trip restores prior decisions + annotations.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the compacted-digest mechanism in ChatHistoryManager; confirm it already covers ledger outputs and keys survive verbatim.</step>
    <step order="2">Verify/adjust the Compose session key to `DocumentId + MatterId` so a new DOCX version (Word save) does not create a new session or reset state.</step>
    <step order="3">On session load after a version change, restore prior decisions + annotations (via task 061 query + task 060 annotations) into the resumed view.</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm workspace-scope memory items are excluded from conversation-window compaction (they persist independently).</step>
    <step order="5">Add tests: version change preserves session state; long session renders from the digest; digest keys survive verbatim.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify build + report publish-size delta (expected ~0).</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Overlaps with the redesign-r1 compacted-digest mechanism and the ChatSession DocumentId binding. Verified both exist.</existing>
    <extension>Extends existing binding/digest by keying Compose sessions version-independently and consuming the existing digest — no new compaction path or store.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without DocumentId+MatterId keying, a Word save (new DOCX version) resets the session — the user loses all prior decisions and annotations on return-from-Word, defeating the memory-continuity moat.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — DocumentId+MatterId keying + restore</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/CrossVersionSessionPersistenceTests.cs</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Compose session state is keyed by `DocumentId + MatterId`, independent of DOCX version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A DOCX version change (Word save) does not reset or fork the session (test-verified).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Long sessions render from the compacted digest over ledger outputs; digest keys survive verbatim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Workspace-scope memory items are unaffected by conversation-window compaction.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reopening after a Word round-trip restores prior decisions + annotations; unit tests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-09. Verified (no code change needed) that the redesign-r1 compacted
    digest (ChatHistoryManager.BuildOutputDigestSection) already generalizes over EVERY
    SessionOutput disposition, including `compose` — Compose rides it with zero special-casing,
    satisfying "no parallel compaction path" (ADR-040).

    Implemented the DocumentId+MatterId cross-version binding in
    `ComposeService.LoadAsync` via two new private static helpers, `IsSameCrossVersionBinding`
    and `BuildMatterHostContext`: a resumed session must match the existing version-independent
    DocumentId binding (bindingId — task 060) AND, when the caller supplies one, the session's
    Matter (carried on the EXISTING `ChatSession.HostContext`, EntityType `"matter"` — no new
    stored field). A null MatterId preserves the FR-29 DocumentId-only match unchanged (backward
    compatible). Also wired task 061's `GetActionHistory` query into the restored
    `LoadComposeDocumentResult.ActionHistory` so "prior decisions" restore alongside "prior
    annotations" on a resumed load.

    SCOPE NOTE (flagged transparently, not hidden): implementing `MatterId` (request) and
    `ActionHistory` (result) required adding two optional/backward-compatible properties to
    `LoadComposeDocumentRequest`/`LoadComposeDocumentResult` in
    `Services/Compose/IComposeService.cs` — outside the dispatch prompt's literal
    ComposeService.cs-only file list, but inside the same Services/Compose/ C# domain (no
    frontend `.ts`/`.tsx`, no `.claude/` touched). Necessary because those DTOs are declared in
    that file; without the addition the DocumentId+MatterId acceptance criterion would not be
    testable end-to-end. `ComposeEndpoints.cs` (the actual HTTP query-param wiring for MatterId)
    was intentionally NOT touched — out of this task's scope; a follow-up should wire the query
    param when a caller needs to pass MatterId over the wire.

    New tests: `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/CrossVersionSessionPersistenceTests.cs`
    (9 tests) — version-change-preserves-session, MatterId match/mismatch/backward-compat,
    new-session HostContext seeding, action-history restore, empty-history negative case, digest
    verbatim-key-survival (against the real ChatHistoryManager.TriggerSummarisationAsync), and a
    structural ADR-015 assertion that ChatHistoryManager has no Memory Service dependency. All
    green; full Compose suite (162 tests) + ADR-013 Tier-1 NetArchTest facade test green.

    Quality gates (Step 9.5, mandatory per CLAUDE.md §8 test-modifying override): code-review
    and adr-check both run — 0 Critical, 0 Violations. code-review raised 1 Warning (the scope
    note above, self-flagged) + 2 Suggestions (minor comment clarity); adr-check found 0
    violations across ADR-013/040/015/010.

    Publish size: 46 MB compressed (tar.gz) incl. PDBs — at/under the ~49.63 MB incl-PDB
    baseline; zero packages added, delta ~0 as expected. CVE scan: same pre-existing
    Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions HIGH advisory (GHSA-7j59-v9qr-6fq9) as baseline — not
    introduced by this task, no new HIGH/Critical CVE.

    No deferrals filed — all 5 acceptance criteria met.
  </notes>
</task>
